From: TDVP maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] pkg_hash: preserve Essential held base file ownership

Historical runtime packages may retain file lists overlapping the held image
base. Initializing the ownership hash must not transfer those base files to
an unprotected package: later upgrade or removal would unlink the base files
and rewrite their Essential owner's list.

Give existing Essential+hold ownership priority for regular files and
symlinks to files. An Essential+hold owner loaded later can still reclaim a
file from an unprotected package. Shared directory behavior and ordinary
ownership transfer are unchanged. Normal install conflict checks continue
to reject new payloads attempting to overwrite protected files.

Upstream-Status: Pending
--- a/libopkg/pkg_hash.c
+++ b/libopkg/pkg_hash.c
@@ -921,6 +921,14 @@
     if (old_owning_pkg == owning_pkg)
         return;
 
+    /* Historical package lists must not displace protected base files. */
+    if (old_owning_pkg && old_owning_pkg->essential
+        && (old_owning_pkg->state_flag & SF_HOLD)
+        && !(owning_pkg->essential && (owning_pkg->state_flag & SF_HOLD))
+        && !file_is_dir(long_file_name)
+        && !file_is_symlink_to_dir(long_file_name))
+        return;
+
     hash_table_insert(&opkg_config->file_hash, file_name, owning_pkg);
 
     /*
